      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s right. Since multiple vendors use the virtio-balloon driver and the VM memory size might vary, this patch set aims at starting a discussion on we can agree on modifying the virtio-balloon prdev order.\n\nSome approaches that I have in my mind for run-time order changing:\n1) Make virtio-balloon order a function of memory size.\n\n2) The order can start off at MAX_PAGE_ORDER and can be reduced if free-page-reporting driver is not able to find any order sized pages in all zones\u0027 free area list. Order can be reset to MAX_PAGE_ORDER when these big chunks are available again.\n\n3) Add a CONFIG_VIRTIO_BALLOON_4K_ORDER (or some better sounding name) to statically control the order when THPs are not a concern.\n\nPlease let me know what you think of these approaches. From what I understand from FPR and balloon, they were designed keeping THP and fairly sized guests and on smaller guests (in our case Qualcomm\u0027s Trusted VM), virtio-balloon stays quiet.",
